# Dance with Inhibition — only small, public-safe code and the frozen reference
# set belong in git. Everything the pipeline produces is large and governed, and
# lives under /data/lab_vm/{immutable,append_only}/inhibition instead.
#
# Risk R9 in the plan: large data leaking into GitHub. security_guard gates
# every push; this file is the first line of that defence.

# --- generated candidate frames and shortlists (governed data root) ---
*.parquet
*.sdf
*.mol2
*.pdbqt
D[1-4].csv
D[1-4]_top10.csv

# --- structures, poses, trajectories ---
*.pdb
*.xtc
*.trr
*.dcd
*.rst7
*.prmtop
*.inpcrd
poses/
trajectories/

# --- model weights and fragment databases (immutable/) ---
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.db
weights/
fragment_db/

# --- tool scratch ---
*.log
manifest.json
enrichment_gate.token
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

# --- environments ---
.conda/
.venv/
env/

# --- machine-specific ---
.DS_Store
*.local.yaml
.env

# --- EXPLICIT ALLOW: the frozen reference set is the ONLY data committed. ---
# It is small, published, and must travel with the code so a run pins an exact
# version. Negations come last so they win over the patterns above.
!data/reference/
!data/reference/*.csv
!data/reference/.provenance.md

# --- mkdocs build output (regenerate with `mkdocs build`) ---
site/
